<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Savona</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Savona is a port city on the Ligurian coast of north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genoa">Genoa</a>. A rival of Genoa in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a>, it was subdued by the Genoese in 1528. The della Rovere family of Popes Sixtus IV and Julius II came from the area, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> held <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-pius-vii">Pope Pius VII</a> captive in the city from 1809 to 1812.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/savona.jpg" alt="Savona" width="320" height="198" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Roberta Salamone · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Savona_(260099167).jpeg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
